# =============================================================================
# Line endings
#
# 🚨 `scripts/*.mjs` MUST be checked out with LF, and this is not cosmetic.
#
# Every one of them opens with `#!/usr/bin/env node`. Vite's SSR transform —
# the one vitest runs — hoists its `__vite_ssr_import__` / export shims ABOVE
# the module's first line, and its hashbang strip does not account for a CRLF
# ending. With CRLF the shims and the `#!` land on ONE line, so the module
# compiles to `…shims…#!/usr/bin/env node` and every import of it dies with
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`, reported against the IMPORTING
# file and with no location.
#
# `src/ui/typeScale.test.js` — the codemod's guard — statically imports six of
# these. On Windows, where git's `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, the whole guard therefore failed to LOAD: `npx vitest run` reported
# 139 files / 2823 tests with one failed suite, where CI (Linux, LF) reported
# 140 / 2858 green. A guard that cannot be imported is the same defect the two
# adversarial rounds kept finding one level down — an assertion that cannot
# fail — except that it cannot even run.
#
# The blobs are already LF in the object store (autocrlf converts on checkout,
# not on commit), so this pins the checkout and changes no content.
# =============================================================================
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
